course: dictionary
lesson: 12109
title: Coldness: cold air and cold feelings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word coldness comes from cold. The ending -ness turns cold into a noun, a word for a thing or state. Coldness has two meanings. The first is about temperature: «The coldness of the lake took her breath away.»
explain: The second is about people. Coldness can mean unfriendly behaviour, when someone does not show warmth, kindness or interest. «His coldness towards the new boy made everyone feel unwelcome.» Here the clue is the new boy feeling unwelcome, so coldness means unfriendliness, not temperature.
explain: To choose the right meaning, read the words around coldness and then try your meaning in the sentence. If «low temperature» fits, use it. If it sounds strange, try «unfriendly behaviour».
fact: Coldness is a noun, and you usually do not count it, so you say «the coldness», not «a coldness».
fact: Coldness means the state of being cold, with a low temperature.
fact: Coldness can also mean unfriendly behaviour: not showing warmth, kindness or interest.
fact: You can say «treat someone with coldness», which means to be unfriendly to them.
fact: Science lessons often say «cold» or «low temperature», but «the coldness of the ice» is also used in descriptions.
exercise: «The coldness of the lake took her breath away.» What does coldness mean here? | Kindness and warmth | *The low temperature of the water | A loud noise | Fast movement
exercise: «Her coldness towards him made him feel unwelcome.» What does coldness mean here? | Having a low temperature | Shouting at people | Being very tired | *Unfriendly behaviour
exercise: Which phrase means to be unfriendly to someone? | treat someone with a map | treat someone with a song | treat someone with delight | *treat someone with coldness
test: «The coldness of the ice cream made my teeth ache.» What does coldness mean? | Unfriendly behaviour | *Low temperature | Surprise | Tiredness
test: «After the argument, Sam showed coldness to his best friend.» What does coldness mean? | Bright light from the sun | A long walk in the rain | *Being unfriendly and distant | A loud, angry shout
exam: «The coldness in the room came from the open window, but the coldness in her voice came from anger.» What does the second coldness mean? | Happy feelings | Low temperature of the room | Wet weather | *Unfriendly, distant behaviour
